# Phase 7.5 BUILD-B — Stage A PASS (QEMU): the Phase-4 stack over USB
# Scenario: usb_ethernet (qemu-xhci + usb-net on a slirp user netdev)
# Date: 2026-06-12. Branch: codex/phase-7.5-build-B-usb-ethernet-jarvis.
#
# What this run proves (ISC-15/16, ADR-047):
# - QEMU's usb-net (0525:a4a2, DUAL-config) enumerates, the ECM function is
#   found BY CONTENT (config 1, comm if 0 / data if 1 alt 1, maxseg 1514),
#   and cdc-ecm claims it through the 7.5-A seam.
# - MAC parsed from the iMACAddress string descriptor (52:54:00:12:34:56).
# - The FS-device Evaluate-Context dance (the BUILD-A silicon lesson) fired
#   in QEMU too: MPS0=64 vs FS default 8.
# - REAL DORA over the bulk pipes: DISCOVER/REQUEST egressed bulk-OUT,
#   slirp's OFFER/ACK arrived bulk-IN (census: offer=1 ack=1), lease
#   10.0.2.15 applied. ARP resolved on the wire (arp=1). DNS round-trip to
#   10.0.2.3 (udp53=1) — and AGAIN after the flood leg (post-flood alive).
# - Kill-switch (ISC-10): cdc_ecm disabled ⇒ probe-only re-offer matches 0
#   drivers (BUILD-A's branch); re-enabled ⇒ matches again.
# - RX-flood (ISC-12 / I-14(b)): 512 synthetic events through the REAL
#   routing path → queue ≤ EP_QUEUE_CAP(64), drops=448 — EXACTLY 512−64.
# - link_state rode the interrupt endpoint genuinely (14 NetworkConnection
#   notifications — no assume-up fallback needed in QEMU).
# - Containment: fence refusals 0, span leaks 0, ISR cap held, ep_errors 0,
#   tx=5/tx_completed=5/rx=5 balanced.
#
# Found-and-fixed during this gate (the changelog trail):
# - The byte oracle (ISC-1a) refuted the first parser draft on first run:
#   wMaxSegmentSize read at bytes 10..12 instead of 8..10 (after the 4-byte
#   bmEthernetStatistics). A writer-paired round-trip would have agreed
#   with the shared mistake — the ADR-028 rule, demonstrated live.
# - Gate run 1: device fully bound, pump census frames=0 — the poll-
#   starvation signature. qemu-xhci delivers no MSI (msi_configured=false)
#   and BUILD-A only drained inside enumeration wait loops; the F6 poll
#   path is now production (xhci::poll_events) on the class-driver service
#   path. Run 2 passed end-to-end.
# - BUILD-A hub path dropped its device context with DCBAA[slot] still set
#   (latent on silicon); every path now clears before drop (Anti-3).
#
